Now we can plug $\blueD{\theta=\dfrac{\pi}{2}}$ into the expression we got:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}-\dfrac{8}{\blueD{\left(\dfrac{\pi}{2}\right)}^2}\sin\blueD{\left(\dfrac{\pi}{2}\right)}+\dfrac{8}{\blueD{\left(\dfrac{\pi}{2}\right)}}\cos\blueD{\left(\dfrac{\pi}{2}\right)}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{32}{\pi^2}(1)+\dfrac{16}{\pi}(0)
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{32}{\pi^2}
\end{align}$
